# NickelHome (libnickelhome.so)
#
# This mod tweaks the Kobo home screen by hiding specific widgets after the
# home view is constructed. It is built on NickelHook and is a sibling of
# NickelMenu (https://pgaskin.net/NickelMenu).
#
# It should work on firmware 4.23.15505+ (the version which introduced the
# current home screen layout). It is safe to try on newer firmware: if a widget
# is not found on the running firmware, it is silently skipped and a warning is
# written to syslog (view it with `logread`). A failsafe mechanism automatically
# uninstalls the mod as a last resort if Nickel fails to start.
#
# Configuration lives in a single file at:
#
#   KOBOeReader/.adds/nickelhome/config
#
# Each line is either blank, a comment (starting with #), or an option in the
# form:
#
#   <key>:<val>
#
# Spaces around fields are ignored. If an option is declared more than once,
# only the first declaration takes effect. A reboot is required for changes to
# take effect.
#
# These options hide elements on the home screen by their internal widget name.
# They are the runtime equivalent of the corresponding kobopatch patches.
#
#   <key>  one of:
#            hide_home_row1col2_enabled - hides the recommendations column in the top-right
#                                         of the home screen, next to the book you are
#                                         currently reading (when fewer than 2 books are open)
#            hide_home_row2col2_enabled - hides the `row2col2` quick tour card on the home
#                                         screen; this is a visual-only hide which disables
#                                         the widget and makes it transparent without collapsing
#                                         its layout space so "My Books" doesn't break
#            hide_home_row2_enabled     - hides both "My Books" and the quick tour card;
#                                         your books should still be accessible via the
#                                         appropriate navigation tab (unless also hidden)
#            hide_home_row3_enabled     - hides the footer row below "My Books" on the home
#                                         screen, which often advertises features like the
#                                         Kobo Store, Pocket, and more
#   <val>  0 or 1
#
# Example:
#   hide_home_row1col2_enabled:1
#   hide_home_row2col2_enabled:1
#   hide_home_row2_enabled:0
#   hide_home_row3_enabled:1
#
# To uninstall NickelHome, create a new (empty) file named `uninstall` in
# KOBOeReader/.adds/nickelhome/, then reboot. You can also trigger the failsafe
# mechanism by immediately powering off the Kobo after it starts booting.
